<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31236" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἷς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίᾰ,
		ἕν</span> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίη</span> only in late 
			Ion.
		 Prose): gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑνός, μιᾶς, ἑνός</span>:—
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕεις</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Hes.
			<u>Th.</u>
			145
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			7.341
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			Procl.
		</span></i>), cj.in <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			5.603
		</span></i>:—
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧς</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Rhinth.
			12
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Tab.Heracl.</u>
			1.136
		</span></i>:—
			Ep.
		, 
			Aeol.
		, and 
			Ion.
		 fem. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴᾰ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.354
				</span></i>
			, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Morb.</u>
				4.37
			</span></i>; acc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alc.
					33.6
				</span></i>
			(prob.), <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				69.1
			</span></i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδεΐα</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Corinn.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				2.56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(2).517.22
			</span></i>(Thess.); gen.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.173
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				24.496
			</span></i>; dat. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.319
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				11.174
			</span></i>, etc.: neut. dat. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰῷ κίον
				ἤματι</span>)<i><span class="en">
				6.422
			</span></i>. (In Com. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ
				ʽμηδἒ εἷς, οὐδὲ
				ʽμηδἒ ἕν,</span> occur, mostly at the
			end of an iambic trimeter, without elision, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				302
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				927
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pl.</u>
				37
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				138
			</span></i>,al.) (Orig. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕνς</span></b> ,
			assim. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔν</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ</span>) prob. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Leg.Gort.</u>
				9.50
			</span></i>, from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἕμς,</span>
			I.-Eur. <i>sem</i>-(cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμός</span>);
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μία</span> from <i>sm</i>-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ία</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴα</span>
			is not related to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μία,</span> but prob. to
			pronom. stem <i>i</i>-(Lat.<i>is</i>), cf.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰός.</span>) </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			as a Numeral, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἷς
		κοίρανος</span></div>
